    {
      "index": 0,
      "part": {
        "content": "Let me analyze this case. The customer received a product in a dented box, but the main issues are flickering near the controller and overheating after 30 minutes of use. The customer is concerned about safety and wants a warranty resolution.\n\nThe dented box could suggest delivery damage, but the flickering and overheating are functional issues that appeared during use. The overheating is a safety concern. The customer wants a warranty resolution, which points to a defect claim rather than a delivery claim.\n\nThe dented box might have caused damage, but the primary intent seems to be defect - the product is malfunctioning (flickering, overheating) and the customer wants warranty resolution. The safety risk is flagged.\n\nI'll classify this as \"defect\" with high confidence.",
